Z||000004||kslish||12-05-2000||03:36 AM||||Sheesh, where was that skirt and top outfit (the one on the main page of your site) at Carlisle last year?  Guess it was too cold or something....  Now I know why you win all those awards at the Daytona show and so on.  j/k  The cars look great.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Nice GT by the way, a lot nicer than mine.  I'll probably be at the shows with the 4-cyl coupe again next year.  At least the the paint job is finally completely finished on that one.  One of these days I'll get post a web site with some pics so everyone can see the resurrection project my GT is.  Or come see it at Fieros at Carlisle 2004 (which is when I'll finally have it done at the rate I'm going).  <P>All it takes is time and $$$.  And maybe year-round warm weather.....and did I mention $$$?<P>Ken S.<BR>'86 SC and '87 GT<P>P.S. - What is up with you and gold Fieros anyways?  <p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 12-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroLisa||12-05-2000||10:52 AM||||Don't know what the deal is with me and gold Fieros- GT won't be gold for too long. I'm searching for someone to do the perfect paint job...this requires more patience than I have. Won't be done by Daytona, but if the coupe isn't sold by then, there's a strong chance BOTH my gold cars will be there.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/||||reg||1
Z||000006||kslish||12-05-2000||04:07 PM||||Never seen somebody actually take TWO cars a long distance to a show before.  If both of mine were finished it would be a hard decision to decide which to drive.<P>What color are you planning on changing the GT to?<P>Some tips I have found (from personal experience) on getting a good paint job:<P>If you have to go to a large multi-employee body shop, slip the guy that is actually doing to work some extra $$$ under the table to be "extra careful."  <P>If you go to a small shop (my preference) don't be in a hurry to get the car back, let them rush other people's jobs but not yours.  My painter had my '86 Fiero for a month painting it the first time, and over a week the time I had some scratched panels fixed.  A month was probably a little extreme but I let him work at his own pace.  <P>Also go when they aren't too backed up with insurance jobs and so on (which is their bread and butter).  When a painter doesn't have any other jobs pending they don't mind taking the extra time to do the job right.<P>My GT is going to be resprayed by a retired guy that restores Corvettes in his spare time, but I have to wait until his Vette work slows down....the price is right though, $850 for factory basecoat/clearcoat in medium red metallic and the work will be impeccable.<P>Ken S.<BR>'86 SC and '87 GT<BR>||||reg||1
